by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-14T13:54:49Z

Argument order and the `UPGRADE-8.2.md` merge look good to me. A few things:

1. `$this->isHandling = true` is set before `getConnections()`, which sits outside the `try`/`finally` that resets it. When it throws (unknown name, non-DBAL connection) the flag stays true, so every later message takes the re-entrancy early return and the middleware silently stops logging for the rest of the worker's life. Setting the flag after the two resolution lines fixes it.

2. The `DoctrineDbalCloseConnectionMiddleware` changes look out of scope here. Moving `getConnections()` into the `finally` also means a misconfigured name now fails after the handler ran, and an exception coming from the handler is demoted to `previous` while `UnrecoverableMessageHandlingException` surfaces, which Messenger will not retry. I would drop that hunk, docblock removal included.

3. `@param list<string>|string $connectionNames or none to close them all` is copied from the close middleware; this one does not close anything.

4. Worth covering the default "no names, every connection" path, since that is the headline change in the upgrade note, plus the case where no transaction is left open.

